notes:
Hypervisor - Acts as a referee between lab machines and allows each virtual computer to behave independently.
Virtual computer/lab machine - Acts as an independent system with it's own operating system, programs, and settings even though they all share the same physical hardware underneath.
Two types of hypervisors:
  Type 1 - Run directly on physical hardware making them efficient. Useful for database servers and data centers.
  Type 2 - Run within an existing operating system making them easy to install. Useful for learning and testing.

Virtualisation simply:
  The building = the physical server
  The apartments = lab machines
  The tenants = applications or operating systems
  The building manager = the hypervisor (divides the building safely)



